WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:08.710
Drinking tonic diluted in water
is said to prevent malaria.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:37.590
Seriously! Why'd it have to start raining?

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:41.720
Here we go. A shelter from the rain.

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:46.140
What's this all about?

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:48.640
Has someone booked out the place?

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:50.860
Young lady, you might as well forget it.

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:51.650
Huh?

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.440
As you see, he's shut shop for today.

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:58.400
That place is reserved for just
one customer, tonight.

00:01:59.110 --> 00:02:00.410
Just one customer?

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:01.410
Yep.

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:05.870
The Glass of the Gods is keeping
the place open for the first customer

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:07.910
to whom he served the wrong cocktail.

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:12.790
Every now and then,

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:18.010
the falling rain creates
a mirror they call "Ginza".

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:22.140
What is reflected is happiness, laughter,

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:24.430
anger and sadness.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:27.350
In this town, a myriad of faces appear

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:29.480
only to then disappear.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:31.350
But tonight,

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:35.650
we will hear the story of the sad face

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:40.950
that surfaces once each year
for the Glass of the Gods.

00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:43.990
MR RYU SASAKURA

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:48.540
No way.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:51.370
I can't believe Mr Sasakura
would serve anybody the wrong cocktail.

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:55.540
That guy's not always been
the Glass of the Gods, you know.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:58.590
You've made mistakes too, right?

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:01.090
Well, sure. Lots...

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:06.890
It was just after the kid had
come back from France, I reckon.

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:09.730
You heard of Bar Saito?

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:12.440
Sure. It's one of Ginza's oldest haunts.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:16.230
He was working there at one point.

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:20.780
Gordon's Orange gin?

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:24.740
I thought they'd stopped selling
these back in the 30s.

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:27.830
Hey. Don't go throwing it out
because it's empty, okay?

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:31.330
It's got special memories for
the customer we're receiving tonight.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:35.580
Of course. You don't see
these very often nowadays, right?

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:39.510
It had been a while since he'd been
in a Japanese bar.

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:43.010
And most of all, Bar Saito's owner
had helped him out a lot.

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:44.720
So he was keen on the place.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:48.720
Welcome, Mr Minegishi.

00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:54.560
Hello my friend, you remember Kanako?

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:56.150
Of course he did.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:00.360
Anyone who hadn't heard of Epoire's most
famous hostess wasn't from Ginza.

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:01.990
Welcome.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:03.820
Thank you.

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:06.990
Young man, are you new here?

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:10.080
I am. My name is Ryu Sasakura.

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:12.160
Sasakura, you say.

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:14.620
Much obliged, sir.

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:19.670
Minegishi industries. President - Ryuichi Minegishi.

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:21.800
Everybody in Ginza knew who he was.

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:24.880
He was the face of Ginza, one might say.

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:27.800
A drink for the lady, please.

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:28.890
In that case,

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:32.390
how about a champagne and fruit cocktail?

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:37.060
A peach and champagne Bellini?

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:39.190
Using orange would make it a Mimosa.

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:42.110
Today, you will be tasting
something a little different.

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:49.370
PIease, enjoy. I have attempted
to match the lady's attire.

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:50.830
My oh my.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:54.710
Champagne, grapefruit juice,
and with this...

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.210
Oh... Cherry blossom liqueur.

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:01.500
We also have chestnut, persimmon
and red bean paste flavour.

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:04.840
Combining a seasonal touch
to the presentation,

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:06.840
with a service fit for
a woman's sensibilities.

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:09.390
As expected from Ginza's top bartender...

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:15.600
But spring is over.

00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:20.820
Will you come and drink it again,
next year?

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:24.570
I will do my best.

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:28.780
"Again, next year."

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:33.200
Back then, he hadn't puite
understood what that meant.

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:38.580
And that was bartender
Ryu Sasakura's first mistake.

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:41.090
Young man.

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:43.050
Young man...

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:44.630
Yes, ma'am.

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:47.760
A cocktail with champagne in it, please.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:48.590
Certainly.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:58.440
A champagne Pick-Me-Up.

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:01.940
And cut!

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:05.360
And there was his second mistake.

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:09.660
So, you're saying that was the mistaken
cocktail the Glass of the Gods served?

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:11.320
Unfortunately not. Not by a long way.

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:16.250
As a woman, you should have been
able to pick up on that doozy.

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:18.330
What? But...

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:20.330
Here you go. The usual.

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:23.500
Okay, never mind.
Let's keep the story going.

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:25.880
I'll have something else.

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:29.010
Is there something wrong?

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:32.550
Very well.

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:35.930
This was our mistake
so it won't go on your bill.

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:37.270
Mistake?

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:41.270
How would you like to try the drink
we call the face of the bar, instead?

00:06:41.980 --> 00:06:43.190
The face of the bar?

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:47.440
A drink to show the true face of
the bar. That sounds intriguing.

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:48.490
Quite.

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:52.530
First, we squeeze some lime
and add two or three ice cubes.

00:06:52.990 --> 00:06:55.030
45 ml of gin.

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:58.120
And then fill with tonic water.

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:00.870
Finally, a single stir.

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:04.960
Please, enjoy our Gin and Tonic.

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:08.960
Is that the face of the bar?

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:13.930
Indeed. The gin and tonic recipe
changes completely from bar to bar.

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:16.600
Though they have the same name,
they taste completely different.

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:18.520
That's not all Kanako.

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:25.270
The word "tonic" also has
the meaning of "re-energising".

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:26.480
Am I right?

00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:30.990
Yes, indeed. It is the bitterness
that has that effect.

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:36.120
The bitterness originally comes from puina
which was an Incan remedy for fever.

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:41.160
It is still used even now
in some tonic waters.

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:48.000
It gives one energy because it was
once used as a medicine, then?

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:54.470
I could drink medicine that
tastes this good every day.

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:57.350
Right then, Kanako.
Shall we head to the club?

00:07:57.970 --> 00:07:59.010
Yes, dear.

00:07:59.890 --> 00:08:02.890
I'm sorry about the cocktail I served you.

00:08:03.310 --> 00:08:05.400
But would you mind telling me
what was wrong with it?

00:08:06.230 --> 00:08:08.570
And Mr Minegishi...
You barely touched yours.

00:08:09.070 --> 00:08:11.940
Mr Sasakura, please collect the bill.

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:14.740
Of course.

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:17.240
We had a great time, my boy.

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:19.740
Thank you, sir.

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:23.330
The bill's almost 100,000 yen?

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:26.750
They've barely been
in the bar for half an hour!

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:28.420
Now then, Mr Sasakura,

00:08:28.670 --> 00:08:30.130
Iet's see the president out.

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:40.970
This isn't to excuse him but
I suppose anyone might be surprised.

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:46.480
But is Bar Saito really
that kind of place?

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:49.770
To him, at least,
that's how it must have looked.

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:54.530
After that, Mr Minegishi would come
every month during the winters.

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:58.570
I've brought an old friend with me today.

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:01.660
I'm on my own this evening,
is that okay?

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:04.370
It's cold as ever out there.

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:09.420
This might all be puite surprising
to a rookie like yourself.

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:13.920
Ginza's a great place.
Everything about it is great.

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:16.050
I'll be off then.

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:18.550
Keep the change, lad.

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:20.760
Yes, sir.

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:26.890
Of course, he wasn't the kind of fellow
who could keep such things to himself.

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:30.400
In the end, he pulled the owner up on it.

00:09:31.940 --> 00:09:33.030
I see.

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:38.030
So, you thought I might be swindling
a rich customer out of his money?

00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:44.700
Sure, he's a money-spending president
who's been a Ginza regular for many years.

00:09:45.370 --> 00:09:49.040
A loyal customer who hardly touches his
drink, but will pay around 100,000 for it.

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:51.920
That would be normal
in a club in Ginza, but...

00:09:52.210 --> 00:09:53.880
Bars are not clubs.

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:57.340
You're right. They aren't.
Which is precisely why...

00:09:57.420 --> 00:09:58.180
Huh?

00:09:58.630 --> 00:10:01.140
Say Mr Sasakura, this is a bar.

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:03.970
But just as bars have
many different faces,

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:06.180
so too do their customers.

00:10:07.230 --> 00:10:08.690
Customers' faces?

00:10:08.890 --> 00:10:09.690
Yes.

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:11.940
How about we take a walk?

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:17.190
You remember how I said that Gin and Tonic
had the meaning of re-energising?

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:17.950
I do.

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:22.120
But the important thing
is "revitalising" them.

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:26.500
Many customers start
by ordering a gin and tonic.

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:30.290
So, what does the bartender pour
into that glass?

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:33.540
That depends on whether
they're tired or angry...

00:10:33.670 --> 00:10:35.050
Or perhaps, grieving.

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:38.470
And what they were expecting when
they pushed open the door.

00:10:39.220 --> 00:10:41.760
Is that what the face of the bar
is there to answer...?

00:10:41.890 --> 00:10:43.010
We're here.

00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:46.010
KARAOKE
THE GINZA

00:10:46.970 --> 00:10:52.230
After work, if she's not with a customer,
she'll sing karaoke to let it all out.

00:10:53.770 --> 00:10:56.980
This is the other face of
Ginza's top hostess.

00:10:58.030 --> 00:10:59.950
For a thirty-year-old woman, in Ginza,

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:03.990
it wouldn't be surprising if there were
a few men she'd Iike to have snuffed out.

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:06.870
A thirty-year-old woman, in Ginza.

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:13.250
I get it! Kanako got mad
because of the glass.

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:17.250
The champagne flute makes the bubbles
float up beautifully.

00:11:17.550 --> 00:11:21.800
But having to lift your head up high
to drink it makes neck lines visible.

00:11:24.390 --> 00:11:28.770
That's why ladies drink from shallow
coupes, at cocktail parties and the like.

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:30.270
Bingo!

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:36.730
Indeed. Some customers are more worried
about their wrinkles than their glass.

00:11:36.980 --> 00:11:38.900
Even if she doesn't have any.

00:11:39.150 --> 00:11:41.360
I guess that's women for you.

00:11:41.490 --> 00:11:42.400
Hmm...

00:11:42.610 --> 00:11:45.490
So does that mean we shouldn't care
about the drinks we make

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:49.120
being used for entertainment by some
rich man with no interest in spirits?

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:50.660
A rich man's entertainment?

00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:56.250
You've got it wrong.
Mr Minegishi is far from rich.

00:11:57.710 --> 00:11:58.920
He's as poor as they get.

00:12:06.970 --> 00:12:09.220
Mr Minegishi is poor?

00:12:09.310 --> 00:12:10.180
Yeah.

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:14.520
From what I've heard,

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:18.900
he lives in a cheap apartment
in the suburbs, with his wife.

00:12:19.270 --> 00:12:22.650
His Bickner coat.
The Savile Row tailored suit.

00:12:22.780 --> 00:12:24.320
His Edward Green shoes.

00:12:24.780 --> 00:12:28.410
Those are probably
the sum total of his entire estate.

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:33.410
Come to think of it,
he did always turn up dressed the same.

00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:36.920
He was born with a silver spoon
in his mouth.

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:38.590
He took over his father's firm,

00:12:38.670 --> 00:12:41.380
and borrowed vast sums from
the banks during the bubble era,

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:43.130
but when the dust settled, he was ruined.

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:46.010
Anyone else would just run.

00:12:46.130 --> 00:12:48.050
Hide your assets and declare bankruptcy.

00:12:48.140 --> 00:12:50.470
Put everything in your wife's name
and fake a divorce.

00:12:50.890 --> 00:12:54.060
But trying to pay everything off to
the point of going broke...

00:12:54.180 --> 00:12:55.270
That's pretty stupid.

00:12:55.730 --> 00:12:56.480
So...

00:12:56.770 --> 00:12:58.810
How does he pay, you're wondering?

00:12:59.190 --> 00:13:03.110
He spends the money he earns doing
all his various part-time work.

00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:10.950
Why?

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:14.040
Why does he go to such lengths
just to come into Ginza?

00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:16.120
What's so great about it, anyway?

00:13:17.290 --> 00:13:18.960
What can he possibly get

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:22.000
out of barely taking a sip from his glass
yet dropping a small fortune on it?

00:13:25.420 --> 00:13:26.470
Who knows...?

00:13:27.050 --> 00:13:30.640
Perhaps it reminds him of a time when
he had the world at his feet.

00:13:31.050 --> 00:13:32.680
A pride he can't let go of.

00:13:33.020 --> 00:13:34.980
I don't really understand it either.

00:13:35.770 --> 00:13:37.190
But, whatever the reason,

00:13:37.270 --> 00:13:40.900
a bartender isn't supposed to know
nor does he need to.

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:46.400
It's the bartender's rule to only see
the face the customer chooses to show.

00:13:46.700 --> 00:13:51.280
But how are we supposed to give energy
back to those kinds of people?

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:55.120
If he really is penniless, we ought to be
serving him cheaper drinks?

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:57.040
We shouldn't be encouraging him!

00:13:57.500 --> 00:14:00.750
You can find great tasting spirits in
plenty of other places other than Ginza.

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:05.010
Surely he'd better enjoy his drinks
if he didn't spend as much!

00:14:05.130 --> 00:14:07.420
Mr Sasakura, you're mistaken.

00:14:07.510 --> 00:14:10.140
Customers have a great
many different faces. So...

00:14:10.340 --> 00:14:12.760
No... In that case...

00:14:13.760 --> 00:14:16.560
I choose to have
a different bartender's face.

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:27.570
A different bartender's face...

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:30.070
But his plan had a pitfall.

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:31.660
Indeed.

00:14:32.120 --> 00:14:34.410
The problem came up
after he left that job.

00:14:47.670 --> 00:14:49.010
I remember it well...

00:14:49.090 --> 00:14:52.220
The first night the lights
were turned on at Eden hall.

00:14:55.680 --> 00:14:56.640
Welcome.

00:14:58.020 --> 00:15:00.190
Are you open yet, young man?

00:15:01.020 --> 00:15:02.690
Certainly, sir.

00:15:02.850 --> 00:15:03.940
Thank you.

00:15:11.030 --> 00:15:15.700
The owner of Bar Saito told me last month
that you were opening a new bar,

00:15:15.780 --> 00:15:17.740
so I decided I should come take a look.

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:19.910
Thank you.

00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:22.330
Now then, what do I go for...?

00:15:22.750 --> 00:15:24.540
Erm, if it pleases you, Mr Minegishi,

00:15:24.710 --> 00:15:28.090
there is a drink I've been wanting
to make for you since we last met.

00:15:28.420 --> 00:15:30.340
Really? That sounds interesting.

00:15:30.920 --> 00:15:33.720
In that case, allow me to prepare you
a slightly nostalgic cocktail.

00:15:37.470 --> 00:15:40.180
We begin with
a half shot of apricot brandy.

00:15:40.810 --> 00:15:42.730
Three dashes of grenadine syrup.

00:15:42.940 --> 00:15:44.730
One puarter shot of lemon juice.

00:15:45.020 --> 00:15:47.360
And a quarter shot of orange gin.

00:15:49.860 --> 00:15:52.070
And what do we have?

00:15:57.370 --> 00:15:59.740
PIease enjoy your Moulin Rouge.

00:16:00.330 --> 00:16:03.170
Moulin Rouge, eh? The red windmill.

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:12.130
That flavour... How it takes me back.

00:16:13.130 --> 00:16:14.430
The Belle Epoque.

00:16:14.930 --> 00:16:17.850
The cabarets that keep the smell
of the good old days of Paris.

00:16:18.180 --> 00:16:21.310
Those flamboyant cancan
dancers full of energy

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:23.850
loved by the artist, Toulouse-Lautrec.

00:16:24.600 --> 00:16:27.810
The colour and the taste both
bring back so many memories.

00:16:27.980 --> 00:16:30.320
The flavours of a bygone time.

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:33.490
But this Moulin Rouge is an illusion.

00:16:33.700 --> 00:16:34.950
An illusion?

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:35.860
Yes.

00:16:36.490 --> 00:16:40.540
For the image of the Moulin Rouge,
rather than using other brands,

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:43.160
whose production methods differ,
one should use Gordon's Orange gin.

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:45.830
But as they ended production,

00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:47.830
we can no longer get our hands on it.

00:16:48.630 --> 00:16:50.920
Produced in the Trappist
monastery of Eyguebelle,

00:16:51.380 --> 00:16:58.140
this gin is characterised by its low
alcohol content and sweet flavour.

00:16:58.720 --> 00:17:02.470
And so I have used
an orange liqueur, Grand Marnier,

00:17:02.680 --> 00:17:04.560
to replace the orange gin.

00:17:05.390 --> 00:17:08.690
The flavour is probably quite similar
to the original version,

00:17:09.310 --> 00:17:10.110
but...

00:17:10.820 --> 00:17:12.730
No matter how close you get,

00:17:12.780 --> 00:17:15.820
it will never taste the same as
the one made using Gordon's.

00:17:16.490 --> 00:17:18.410
Hence the illusion...

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:23.290
What is lost to the past cannot
be brought back, right?

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:24.870
It cannot...

00:17:25.210 --> 00:17:28.750
The Moulin Rouge from 100 years ago
with its smokey ambiance and

00:17:28.830 --> 00:17:31.340
noisy cabaret dancers
doesn't exist anymore.

00:17:32.130 --> 00:17:36.340
It is now a smoke-free tourist attraction.

00:17:37.880 --> 00:17:41.680
I suppose that is what happens
as time passes...

00:17:42.260 --> 00:17:45.100
Indeed. We cannot go back in time.

00:17:46.180 --> 00:17:50.440
So, I'd hoped I could make you see
that tomorrow is worth living for, sir.

00:17:55.110 --> 00:17:58.150
I also hope you will forgive
a young man's impudence...

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:01.370
Tomorrow...

00:18:03.660 --> 00:18:05.910
To see that tomorrow is worth living for...

00:18:07.660 --> 00:18:09.920
Truly youth is wasted on the young.

00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:13.880
That you should go to such
trouble over a single customer...

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:16.090
What a wonderful bartender
you are' young man.

00:18:16.840 --> 00:18:18.090
Not at all.

00:18:18.800 --> 00:18:19.590
However,

00:18:20.430 --> 00:18:23.930
youth is cruel, and has no remorse.

00:18:26.180 --> 00:18:28.640
Sorry, but could I have
a glass of champagne?

00:18:29.140 --> 00:18:29.850
Of course.

00:18:30.850 --> 00:18:32.730
Make it a Salon, please.

00:18:33.940 --> 00:18:37.110
I only drink Salon '70.

00:18:38.700 --> 00:18:41.490
So... in the cocktails at Bar Saito...

00:18:43.490 --> 00:18:45.620
If that's true then
that price wasn't that high.

00:18:45.790 --> 00:18:48.410
You might even say 100,000 yen
is on the cheap side.

00:18:53.840 --> 00:18:58.630
There's something I'd like you
to understand, young bartender.

00:18:59.010 --> 00:19:02.390
Memories are proof that we lived.

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:07.810
Success... Failure... One looks back
on it all with rose-tinted glasses.

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:17.530
In this world, there are spirits
which taste like that.

00:19:23.160 --> 00:19:24.910
Thank you for the drink.

00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:29.080
Was that the Glass of the Gods'
mistaken cocktail?

00:19:29.410 --> 00:19:32.040
It's like he did something that was
absolutely unwelcomed.

00:19:32.170 --> 00:19:33.080
No...

00:19:33.880 --> 00:19:38.210
UItimately, no matter what he'd served,
he couldn't tell the flavour anyway...

00:19:38.340 --> 00:19:39.340
-What?
-What?

00:19:44.800 --> 00:19:47.310
My husband, Ryuichi Minegishi, following treatment for an ongoing health issue, passed away on April 6th. I had hoped to tell you sooner but
please accept my apologies in the delay informing you of this news. The funeral took place on April 3th. Thank you for the kindness you showed him.

00:19:48.220 --> 00:19:50.600
But, spring is over, isn't it.

00:19:51.140 --> 00:19:54.100
Will you come and drink it again,
next year.

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:57.440
I will do my best.

00:19:57.570 --> 00:20:00.570
So, the owner of the bar knew all along...

00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:08.370
He was a proud man of Ginza,
until the very end.

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:10.580
And since then...

00:20:10.660 --> 00:20:14.670
on this night, every year,
the bar is reserved for him alone.

00:20:19.750 --> 00:20:20.960
Oh, yes.

00:20:22.760 --> 00:20:26.140
From Bar Saito, on the auspicious
opening of your new bar.

00:20:28.050 --> 00:20:29.850
The name of that bottle was

00:20:30.010 --> 00:20:33.100
"Overture" which also means
"opening chapter".

00:20:33.980 --> 00:20:37.940
It was all to celebrate
a new bartender's first steps.

00:20:41.780 --> 00:20:45.110
So for tonight,
Iet's watch over him from here.

00:20:50.080 --> 00:20:53.160
Hoping he will feel re-energised
in the morning.

00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:58.130
And so...

00:20:58.790 --> 00:21:01.130
He earned his face as a bartender.

00:21:06.430 --> 00:21:13.600
RECIPE: DRY GIN - 45ml
TONIC WATER - To taste

